cff-version: 1.2.0
title: interactor-motion-matching-guest
message: If you use this software or its motion database, please cite it and the upstream sources
  listed under `references`.
type: software
authors:
- &fire
  family-names: Lee
  given-names: K. S. Ernest (iFire)
  alias: fire
  website: https://github.com/fire
repository-code: https://github.com/V-Sekai-fire/interactor-motion-matching-guest
license: MIT
abstract: mm.elf, motion matching as a character controller in a godot-sandbox guest, with a
  database of 51 Kimodo clips (data/kimodo-locomotion) and 21 clips of the O3DE MotionMatching gem
  (data/o3de-motionmatching).
keywords:
- motion matching
- character controller
- godot-sandbox
references:
- type: software
  title: godot-motion-matching
  authors:
  - family-names: Sousa
    given-names: Guilherme
    alias: GuilhermeGSousa
  repository-code: https://github.com/V-Sekai/godot-motion-matching
  license: MIT
  notes: The algorithm this guest ports (pose database, trajectory and bone features,
    normalisation, weighted k-d tree, velocity spring).
- type: software
  title: godot-sandbox
  authors:
  - name: godot-sandbox contributors
  repository-code: https://github.com/V-Sekai-fire/godot-sandbox
  license: BSD-3-Clause
  notes: The RISC-V sandbox that runs mm.elf.
- type: software
  title: interactor-motion-guest
  authors:
  - *fire
  repository-code: https://github.com/V-Sekai-fire/interactor-motion-guest
  license: MIT
  notes: motion.elf, which made the clips in data/kimodo-locomotion.
- type: software
  title: Kimodo
  authors:
  - name: NVIDIA
  repository-code: https://github.com/nv-tlabs/kimodo
  license: Apache-2.0
- type: software
  title: Kimodo-SOMA-RP-v1.1
  authors:
  - name: NVIDIA
  url: https://huggingface.co/nvidia/Kimodo-SOMA-RP-v1.1
  license-url: https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/agreements/enterprise-software/nvidia-open-model-license
  notes: NVIDIA Open Model License. The animation model; the 51 clips in data/kimodo-locomotion are
    its output (50 steps, seed 1171). They are the output of a program; no person recorded them.
- type: software
  title: Llama-3-Kimodo-GGML (LLM2Vec encoder, Meta Llama 3)
  authors:
  - *fire
  - name: Meta
  url: https://huggingface.co/chibifire/Llama-3-Kimodo-GGML
  license-url: https://www.llama.com/llama3/license/
  notes: Meta Llama 3 Community License. Made the prompt embeddings for the clips ahead of time.
    This repository does not contain the encoder or the Llama 3 model. Built with Meta Llama 3.
- type: data
  title: O3DE MotionMatching gem animations
  authors:
  - name: Open 3D Engine contributors
  repository-code: https://github.com/o3de/o3de/tree/development/Gems/MotionMatching/Assets/Animations
  license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - MIT
  notes: Motion capture of the Rin character (walks, jogs, runs, pivots, turns, circles, snake,
    crouching, jumps); 21 of its 22 clips (not Pushes1) moved to SOMA30 by tools/fbx_to_soma.gd
    in data/o3de-motionmatching, with the O3DE licence files.
- type: software
  title: Motion-Matching
  authors:
  - family-names: Holden
    given-names: Daniel
    alias: orangeduck
  repository-code: https://github.com/orangeduck/Motion-Matching
  license: MIT
  notes: The pose-cost candidates facing as a direction vector, normalisation per feature group
    and a transition cost on every switch.
- type: article
  title: Learned Motion Matching
  authors:
  - family-names: Holden
    given-names: Daniel
  - family-names: Kanoun
    given-names: Oussama
  - family-names: Perepichka
    given-names: Maksym
  - family-names: Popa
