  journal: ACM Transactions on Graphics
  volume: 39
  issue: 4
  year: 2020
  doi: 10.1145/3386569.3392440
- type: conference-paper
  title: 'The Right Foot in the Wrong Place: Character Locomotion in Half-Life: Alyx'
  authors:
  - family-names: van den Heuvel
    given-names: Joe
  conference:
    name: SIGGRAPH 2021
  year: 2021
  url: http://media.steampowered.com/apps/valve/2021/Half-Life_Alyx_Locomotion_Slides.pdf
  notes: The pose-cost candidates footbase position, step progression as a 2D vector, trajectory
    samples by distance, the correction counted in the current pose's score and flattened goal
    samples on slopes.
- type: conference-paper
  title: 'WalkTheDog: Cross-Morphology Motion Alignment via Phase Manifolds'
  authors:
  - family-names: Li
    given-names: Peizhuo
  - family-names: Starke
    given-names: Sebastian
  - family-names: Ye
    given-names: Yuting
  - family-names: Sorkine-Hornung
    given-names: Olga
  conference:
    name: SIGGRAPH 2024 Conference Papers
  year: 2024
  doi: 10.1145/3641519.3657508
  notes: The learned phase that mm_clip_phase takes, here from a periodic autoencoder with
    residual FSQ codes in place of its vector-quantised codebook; the phase window and duration
    terms of its frequency-scaled motion matching are pose-cost candidates.
- type: software
  title: interactor-residual-fsq-recommender
  authors:
  - *fire
  repository-code: https://github.com/V-Sekai-fire/interactor-residual-fsq-recommender
  license: MIT
  notes: The residual FSQ codec for the learned phase's curve codes.
- type: article
  title: 'Frontier Learning: Training LLM Reasoners at the Edge of Capability'
  authors:
